+# NOTICE
+
+This directory vendors the **Lemo-Opuscar** engine and 15 selected demo style
+trees, by **Lemomo (LemoLab)** — https://github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar
+(commit `8ca0dd8`).
+
+## Code — MIT
+
+The engine code in `library/core/` and the demo code under
+`library/styles/*/demo/` is licensed under the **MIT License**. The upstream root
+`LICENSE` is vendored verbatim at `LICENSE` (it names LemoLab / SecondFirst Pty
+Ltd and maps the code to MIT); the MIT text itself is kept at `LICENSES-MIT.txt`.
+Copyright is held by **SecondFirst Pty Ltd, trading as LemoLab**.
+
+## Fonts — SIL Open Font License 1.1
+
+The engine font asset in `library/core/fonts/` (`f0.woff2`–`f7.woff2`,
+`fonts.css`) is licensed under the **SIL Open Font License 1.1**; the full text
+and per-family attribution are in `library/core/fonts/OFL.md`. Demo-local font
+licence texts (`styles/*/demo/fonts/*.txt`) are kept with the code they cover.
+
+## Third-party demo media and CAD data — not vendored
+
+Third-party demo media and CAD data were **not vendored**. This includes the Poly
+Haven CC0 assets that upstream ships under `core/assets/polyhaven/` (HDRI maps,
+textures, and glTF/bin models) — the whole `core/assets/` tree was removed — and
+the entire upstream `teardown` demo (KiCad/STEP converter tools, CAD-derived
+`pcb.json`, and the Corne-specific modules), which is not shipped; our v1
+`teardown` is illustrative `parts_spec` only. The `briefing-board` BiRefNet
+segmentation downloader (`kit_env.sh`, `prep_object.py`, `sky_key.py`,
+`rebuild_objects.sh`) and its model references were also removed. Demo media
+generally (`*.jpg`, `*.png`, `*.svg`, `*.gltf`, `*.bin`, `*.hdr`, `*.mp4`,
+`*.wav`, and other binary/audio/3D assets) is stripped and handled per-style in a
+later phase.
+
+## Branded material removed
+
+The upstream `living-screencast` demo was Claude/Clawd-branded. Its branded
+surface was deleted during vendoring; see `UPSTREAM.md`. Provenance docs may
+name the removed branded material, but no vendored code or text file retains it.
+
+## Third-party material
+
+Other upstream material (music, samples, footage, data, third-party marks)
+keeps its own licence or terms. Where a stripped asset is referenced by vendored
+code, the code is kept for Phase 0 and the asset is handled per-style later.
