+Meet Pip — Mid-century Cartoon demo · asset sources & licenses
+
+Artwork      All characters (June, Pip), props, plans, icons and backgrounds drawn procedurally in code (engine/, film.js). No generated images.
+Music        Original score, generated in code (music/score.py). See music/CREDITS_music.txt:
+             Drums: "MuldjordKit" by Lars Muldjord (drumgizmo.org), FreePats version, CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
+             Samples (CC0): Karoryfer Samples / sfzinstruments, VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition and Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios)
+Sound FX     Synthesized in code (mix.py + core/audio/sfx.py). No recorded samples.
+Voice        Kokoro-82M TTS (kokoro-onnx), Apache-2.0 — voice am_michael, speed 0.94.
+Fonts        Oleo Script (Soytutype), Alfa Slab One (JM Solé), Jost (indestructible type*) — SIL Open Font License 1.1, files + licences in fonts/.
+Product      "Pip" and "Mo" are fictional products. No real brand, product, logo or trademark appears.
+Style        Grammar learned from 1950s UPA limited animation, 1950s classroom films and mid-century illustration (Charley Harper, Mary Blair).
+             No character, design, lettering or music from any of them is reproduced.
+
+ON SCREEN
+The CC BY material above is credited on the end card, in fine print held at least 2.5 s: Music: original, played in code on CC0 samples and the “MuldjordKit” drums by Lars Muldjord (CC BY 4.0).
